# Secrets — never commit. The Enable Banking application's private RSA key lives as
# <application-id>.pem; the filename itself is the application ID (TRACER-BULLET.md, step 0).
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*

# .NET build output (backend/, from TRACER-BULLET.md step 1)
bin/
obj/

# Raw bank responses saved by GET /raw (TRACER-BULLET.md step 3). Evidence for the R3a/R10b
# tuning pass — and real account data from step 6 on, so it stays local.
raw/

# The live consent remembered across restarts (backend/GreedyNose.Api/consent.local.json). It
# holds a session id that reads a real bank account — a credential, not a cache. The glob also
# covers consent.local.json.n26-bak, a backup made while swapping to sandbox credentials
# (2026-09-16) — same class of data, just not the live file.
consent.local.json*

# Account exports used to seed the Mock ASPSP (TRACER-BULLET.md, step 3). N26.json is a real
# account's full transaction history — the same class of data as raw/, just arriving by hand.
N26.json
